@startuml
title Course registration — sequence (R1–R5)
actor Student
participant CatalogService
participant RegistrationService
database EnrollmentStore

== Catalog browsing (R1) ==
Student -> CatalogService : browseCatalog(semester)
CatalogService -> EnrollmentStore : listOfferings(semester, course code, title, capacity, count)
EnrollmentStore --> CatalogService : offerings and current counts
CatalogService --> Student : show code, title, offering, available places
note right of CatalogService
  A catalog view does not reserve a place.
  Displayed availability can become stale.
end note

== Select and register ==
Student -> CatalogService : select offering
Student -> RegistrationService : register(student, offering)

critical atomic registration: final checks and creation
  RegistrationService -> EnrollmentStore : existsEnrollment(student, offering)?
  EnrollmentStore --> RegistrationService : duplicate yes/no
  RegistrationService -> EnrollmentStore : getCurrentCountAndCapacity(offering)
  EnrollmentStore --> RegistrationService : current count, capacity

  alt already enrolled
    RegistrationService --> Student : reject("already enrolled")
  else course full
    RegistrationService --> Student : reject("course full")
  else not enrolled and places left
    RegistrationService -> EnrollmentStore : createEnrollment(student, offering)
    EnrollmentStore --> RegistrationService : saved Enrollment; count +1
    RegistrationService --> Student : confirm registration
  end
  note over RegistrationService, EnrollmentStore
    Duplicate check, current capacity check, and creation are one
    atomic operation. Competing requests cannot both claim the last place.
    Rejection paths create no record and do not change the count.
  end note
end
@enduml
